```

This line attempts to instantiate the inner class without having an instance of the outer class first. That’s the core issue here.

To create an object of a non-static inner class, you must first have an instance of the outer class. Then, using that outer instance, you can create the inner class object.

So, the correct way would be to:
1. Create an instance of `PrinterConfig`.
2. Use that instance to create an instance of `PrintEngine`.

Can you think about how to adjust your code to make sure that you first create an instance of the outer class before creating the inner class?

